## What to do, in order

1. Train: `python -m {{ input.sft_module }} --base-model {{ input.base_model_or_checkpoint }} --data-dir {{ input.prepared_data_dir }} --config <the config above, as a file> --save-steps {{ input.save_steps }} --output-dir <your artifacts directory>/round_{{ input.round_index }}`. It writes `checkpoints.json` listing every checkpoint it saved.
2. Tournament: score every saved checkpoint with `python {{ input.eval_script }} --checkpoint-dir <checkpoint> --data-dir {{ input.data_dir }} --output-dir <a scratch directory per checkpoint>`; each run writes `score.json`. Run them one after another: one evaluation engine on the card at a time.
3. Soup: sort the scored checkpoints by step and take the contiguous window of {{ input.soup_k }} with the highest mean score (neighbours on the trajectory, never the top-k by score). Run `python {{ input.soup_script }} --output-dir <your artifacts directory>/round_{{ input.round_index }}_soup <the window's checkpoint directories>` and score the soup the same way. Skip this step when fewer than two checkpoints were scored.
4. The round's winner is whichever of the best single checkpoint and the soup scored higher.

A training crash, a missing `checkpoints.json`, or a checkpoint that will not load is a failure of this round: report it in your final message instead of guessing a score. Never change the config, the data, or the scripts.

